olarity is a key consideration in the formulation of nutritional solutions used in parenteral nutrition, as it affects the overall effectiveness and safety of these solutions.", "GLUCOSADO 5%:Glucosado 5% is an intravenous solution containing 5% glucose, used for hydration and energy supply.", "GLUCOSADO 10%:Glucosado 10% is an intravenous solution containing 10% glucose, providing a higher energy supply for patients.", "GLUCOSADO 15%:Glucosado 15% is an intravenous solution with 15% glucose concentration, used for patients needing significant energy.", "GLUCOSADO 20%:Glucosado 20% is an intravenous solution with 20% glucose, providing substantial energy for patients.", "GLUCOSADO 30%:GLUCOSADO 30% is an intravenous solution containing 30% glucose, specifically designed to meet the intensive energy needs of patients.", "GLUCOSADO 40%:Glucosado 40% is a specialized intravenous glucose solution that contains a concentration of 40% glucose. It is primarily utilized in nutritional support, particularly for patients with critical energy requirements. This solution serves as an essential resource in medical settings, providing necessary energy to individuals who may be unable to meet their nutritional needs through regular dietary intake.", "GLUCOSADO 50%:GLUCOSADO 50% is a specialized intravenous glucose solution that contains a concentration of 50% glucose. It is primarily utilized in nutritional support, offering maximum energy to patients who require it. This solution is designed to meet the energy needs of individuals, particularly in medical settings where rapid energy replenishment is essential.", "PESO AJUSTADO:", "GLUCOSADO 70%:Glucosado 70% is a type of glucose solution with a specific concentration used in nutritional support.", "GLUCOSALINO ½:Glucosalino ½ is a type of saline solution used in nutritional support.", "GLUCOSALINO 1/5:Glucosalino 1/5 is a type of saline solution used in nutritional support.", "GLUCOSALINO 1/3 IBYS®:Glucosalino 1/3 Ibys® is a spec